abstract: >
  ArchaeoTrace is a local-first, open-source QGIS plugin (QGIS 3.22–4.99) for
  human-reviewed vectorization of elevation contours from scanned historical
  topographic maps and experimental linear-TIN DEM and hillshade reconstruction.
  Designed for archaeology, historical GIS, geomorphology, and landscape change
  studies, it pairs multi-scale Ink Centerline extraction, bounded direction-aware
  Live-Wire, cubic Hermite gap bridging, and chromatic/avoidance guidance with
  optional fail-closed local ONNX models while keeping all archival map data on
  the user's machine.
